hello good evening the united states has  called a drone strike it launched in  afghanistan at the end of last month a  tragic mistake officials have confirmed  10 civilians including at least seven  children died in kabul no islamic state  militants were killed general frank  mckenzie the head of u.s central command  says his condolences are with the family  and friends of those who lost their  lives  having thoroughly reviewed the findings  of the investigation and the supporting  analysis by interagency partners i am  now convinced that as many as 10  civilians including up to seven children  were tragically killed in that strike  moreover we now assess that it is  unlikely that the vehicle and those who  died were associated with isis k or were  a direct threat to u.s forces  i offer my profound condolences to the  family and friends of those who were  killed well to washington our u.s  correspondent martha keller and martha  there were reports of this at the time  people on the ground said that it was  family members that were killed and the  u.s denied this and said it was  militants until now  yeah general mckenzie they're saying he  offers his profound condolences to the  families of those who were killed in  that drone strike it's important to note  that as recently as monday the pentagon  was saying that this was a strike based  on good intelligence and they said it  was necessary to provo prevent further  attract attacks on american troops  outside the airport in kabul now this  strike was initiated at a time of  incredibly high tension in kabul just  days after the suicide bombing attack  which killed 13 u.s military members and  scores of afghan civilians on the ground  general mark milley the the chairman of  the joint chief of staffs said in the  wake um of that strike that officials  had very good intelligence and that it  was necessary to prevent further attacks  like that one that we saw outside the  airport  over the period of the last couple of  